{number: 84}
{title: I Know Whom I Have Believed}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I know not why God’s wondrous grace to me He hath made [G7] known,
Nor [C] why, unworthy, Christ in love re-[G7] deemed me for His [C] own.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
But [C] “I know whom I have believed,
And am persuaded that [G7] He is able
To [C] keep that which I’ve com-[F] mitted
Unto [C] Him a-[G7] gainst that [C] day.”
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] I know not how this saving faith to me He did im-[G7] part,
Nor [C] how believing in His Word wrought [G7] peace within my [C] heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] I know not how the Spirit moves, convincing men of [G7] sin,
Re-[C] vealing Jesus thro' His Word, cre-[G7] ating faith in [C] Him.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] I know not when my Lord may come, at night or noonday [G7] fair,
Nor [C] if I walk the vale with Him, or [G7] "meet Him in the [C] air."
{end_of_verse}
